Write, at this ABSOLUTE path:
/home/ben/worktrees/beads/w3_atomic-claim/work/w3_atomic-claim/builds/bd-ok4pr.2.1.1786119304934325447.build.json

one JSON object:

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| `schema` | the number `2` |
| `bead_id` | `"bd-ok4pr.2.1"` |
| `run_id` | `"1786119304934325447"` |
| `changes` | `"committed"` when the run made a tagged commit, `"none"` when it correctly made none. No other value |
| `commits` | list of commit SHAs, no duplicates. `"committed"` → exactly the one `(bd-ok4pr.2.1)`-tagged commit `bdc` made; `"none"` → `[]` |
| `acceptance` | list, one entry per bead Acceptance command, in the bead's order, same length |

Each `acceptance` entry has exactly these four keys, no more:

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| `criterion` | string naming what the command proves |
| `command` | the bead's Acceptance command, character for character |
| `exit` | the number `0` — a nonzero exit is a failed build, not a report |
| `log` | the entry's step log filename (grammar below) |

The acceptance step log you write is
`bd-ok4pr.2.1.1786119304934325447_step{N}.log`, where `N` is the entry's 1-based
position in `acceptance`. It is a name relative to
/home/ben/worktrees/beads/w3_atomic-claim/work/w3_atomic-claim/builds/ (no
`builds/` prefix inside the JSON), it must exist in that ABSOLUTE directory, and
it must be non-empty — a silent command records its command line and exit
status. Nothing else is accepted: `.acceptance1.log`, `.acc1.log`, `.a1.log`,
`.accept1.log` and `_step01.log` all fail.

